0	199	Karel Antonius Lucia Maria Van Miert (Dutch: [ˈkaːrəl vɑ ˈmiːrt]; 17 January 1942 – 22 June 2009) was a Belgian politician of the Different Socialist Party and official of the European Commission.



199	209	Biography

209	237	He was born in Oud-Turnhout.
238	324	He studied at Ghent University (1962–1966) and gained a degree in diplomatic sciences.
325	426	In 1976 he became adjunct-national secretary of the – at that time – unitary Belgian socialist party.
427	496	Two years later he became president of the Different Socialist Party.
497	613	In 1989 he was appointed European commissioner responsible for transport, credit and investment and consumer policy.
614	672	In 1992 he was also put in charge of environmental policy.
673	723	On 26 May 1992 he was appointed Minister of State.
724	841	From 1993 till 1999 he served as vice-chairman of the European commission and was responsible for competition policy.
842	938	In this period Van Miert was according to The Guardian "one of the most powerful men in Europe."
939	981	In 2001, he was awarded the Vlerick Award.
982	1061	He also worked with Eli Lilly and Company, a global pharmaceutical corporation.
1062	1153	After his departure from politics Van Miert was an international advisor to Goldman Sachs.

1153	1288	On 22 June 2009, 67-year-old Van Miert died at his home in Beersel, after falling from a garden ladder when he had a cardiac arrest.



1288	1438	Political curriculum
Member of the European Parliament (1979–1985)
Deputy in the Belgian Chamber (1985–1988)
European Commissioner (1989–1999)


